.TH DIFFALLA-PATCH 1 "November 2025" "diffalla 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffalla\-patch \- create, apply, or revert patches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffalla patch create
\fISOURCE\fR \fIDESTINATION\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B diffalla patch apply
\fIPATCH\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B diffalla patch revert
\fIPATCH\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create patches that transform directories, apply patches to target directories, or revert previously applied patches.
.PP
Patches are stored as SQLite databases containing:
.IP \(bu 2
Operations (add, remove, modify, move)
.IP \(bu 2
File content (small files inline, large files in cache)
.IP \(bu 2
Optional revert data for rollback
.SH COMMANDS
.SS patch create
Creates a patch describing how to transform SOURCE to DESTINATION.
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Output patch file path (required)
.TP
.B \-\-reversible
Include revert data for rollback support (increases patch size)
.SS patch apply
Applies a patch to transform a directory.
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show operations without applying changes
.TP
.B \-\-force
Force apply even if validation fails
.SS patch revert
Reverts a previously applied patch.
.PP
Requirements:
.IP \(bu 2
Patch must be reversible (created with \-\-reversible)
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show operations without reverting
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a patch:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla patch create /v1.0 /v1.1 \-o update\-1.0\-to\-1.1.patch
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a reversible patch:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla patch create /old /new \-o changes.patch \-\-reversible
.fi
.RE
.PP
Apply a patch:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla patch apply update.patch /target/directory
.fi
.RE
.PP
Dry-run to preview changes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla patch apply update.patch /target \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Revert a patch:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffalla patch revert changes.patch /target
.fi
.RE
.SH STORAGE
.PP
File content storage:
.IP \(bu 2
Files <1MB: Stored inline in patch database
.IP \(bu 2
Files ≥1MB: Stored in ~/.cache/diffalla/ with UUID reference
.PP
This hybrid approach optimizes for:
.IP \(bu 2
Small patches: Single-file portability
.IP \(bu 2
Large patches: Efficient storage and memory usage
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Operational error (patch not reversible, target mismatch)
.TP
.B 2
Usage error
.TP
.B 3
File system error
.SH FILES
.TP
.I *.patch, *.db
Patch files (SQLite databases)
.TP
.I ~/.cache/diffalla/
Cache directory for large file content
.SH NOTES
.PP
Reversible patches store original file content, significantly increasing patch size. Use only when rollback is required.
.PP
Patches created from snapshots don't have source file content and cannot include revert data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffalla (1),
.BR diffalla\-compare (1),
.BR diffalla\-export (1),
.BR diffalla\-sync (1)
